+.. option:: --max-overall-connection-per-origin=<NUM>
+
+  Maximum HTTP(S) connections to one origin across all downloads in the
+  process. An origin is the scheme, hostname, and effective port. This
+  limit applies in addition to :option:`--max-connection-per-server <-x>`.
+  Active connections and connection attempts share the limit. Idle
+  connections can be reused or closed to make room for new connections.
+  ``0`` disables the connection limit. A positive ``Retry-After`` in a
+  429 or 503 response applies to new requests to the same hostname
+  independently of this limit, up to 600 seconds. When tasks are waiting,
+  an active download can release a connection at a completed piece if
+  the response supports ranges. Default: ``16``
+
